+## Remarks
+
+No choice principle or orthonormal basis of an arbitrary $H$ is assumed. The completion here is the specified transfinite sequential-hull construction, whose bounded-extension property is proved in [[lem-choice-free-sequential-hilbert-completion-and-extension]]; it is not an unsupported appeal to completeness of the one-stage Cauchy-sequence quotient. The increasing-index basis enumeration in step 4.1 is conditional on a supplied linearly ordered orthonormal basis. The tensor and exterior constructions themselves require no basis or order on $H$.
